{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":222680,"duration_api_ms":222615,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates Unix utilities in Go from C-source-derived specifications, using AI code generation (mage-claude-orchestrator) and differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Shared libraries in `pkg/` (testutils, sys, format), per-utility implementations in `cmd/`, specs in `docs/`, build targets in `magefiles/`.\n\n**Current state:** All code exists only at generation-merged tags from prior pipeline runs; the working branch has specifications only. Release 00.0 (foundational infrastructure: magefiles, format, sys, testutils) has specs complete but no code on the working branch. Releases 01.1–04.1 have varying spec completeness, no code.\n\n**Current release:** rel00.0 — Batch 0 foundational infrastructure. All four use cases (uc001-magefiles, uc002-format, uc003-sys, uc004-testutils) have specs complete but code not started.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Within it, the three library packages (format, sys, testutils) are independent of each other but all are prerequisites for `cmd/` utilities. By P5 (foundational code before features), `pkg/testutils` is the most foundational — it implements the differential testing harness (DD2) that gates ALL utility verification. The architecture specifies its primary type (DiffTest) and fields explicitly, providing the strongest basis for a well-defined task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/testutils: Implement DiffTest struct and differential runner (rel00.0-uc004)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component, data structures section for DiffTest, design decision DD2)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find and read the testutils PRD -- search for prd*testutils*.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/ (find and read the testutils use case -- search for *uc*testutils*.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (testutils section)\n      - go.mod (module path for package imports)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, runner function, comparison logic, normalization hooks\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Define DiffTest struct with fields for Go binary path, reference binary path, input arguments, stdin data, environment variables, expected exit code, and expected output as specified in the testutils PRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement a runner function that executes both the Go binary and the reference GNU binary with identical stdin, arguments, and environment, capturing stdout, stderr, and exit code from each\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement comparison logic that checks stdout, stderr, and exit code between the two binaries and reports divergences with the triggering input, the expected output (reference binary), and the actual output (Go binary)\n      - id: R4\n        text: Support normalization hooks that transform output before comparison to handle known acceptable differences (e.g., timestamps, path prefixes)\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary exported type is DiffTest per ARCHITECTURE.yaml data structures: 'DiffTest: Go struct in pkg/testutils/ defining a single differential test case with fields for input arguments, stdin, environment, expected exit code, and expected output'\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go per project convention P7 -- named after the primary exported type DiffTest, not the package name testutils\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Differential testing is the primary verification mechanism (ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD2) -- tests compare against Homebrew GNU reference binaries, not hardcoded expected values\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: DiffTest struct is defined with all fields specified in the testutils PRD\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Runner executes two binaries with identical inputs and captures stdout, stderr, and exit code from each\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Divergences between Go and reference binary output are reported with the triggering input, expected output, and actual output\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Normalization hooks can be registered and are applied to output before comparison\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Package compiles successfully (go build ./pkg/testutils/...)\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"8a098b56-0f23-494a-81ea-9986fec496a4","total_cost_usd":0.41256800000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19080,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"output_tokens":11411,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19080,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11411,"cacheReadInputTokens":16066,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19080,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.41256800000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"91476809-42bf-40bf-91cf-53b238601689"}
